  "result": "The gate returned **OK** for `drv.motion.circulating_clockwise_about` on the second of six runs.\n\n**The body:**\n- With d as the vector from r's reference point to a's position, the concept holds when all of:\n  - d × v < 0;\n  - (d × v)² > sin_tol² · |d|² · speed²;\n  - speed > speed_tol.\n- It reads only the four atoms the record claims: `kin.position`, `kin.velocity`, `kin.speed` and `st.region_geometry` (the reference point).\n- A road user standing on the reference point gives a cross product of 0, so the concept is false there, as the contract says.\n\n**Gate runs:**\n1. **`CHECK_FAIL`**: the units check rejected comparing the cross product (m²/s) with a zero that has no unit. I rewrote \"cross product < 0\" as `dx·vy < dy·vx`, which is the same condition without a literal.\n2. **`OK`**: 3 witnesses, 4 names, reads 4 atoms.\n\n**Witnesses:**\n- **Region r:** a roundabout island, the square (−5,−5)–(5,5) m, with its reference point at (0,0).\n- **Road user a:** a car at 10 m/s on a 15 m circle around the island.\n- **Instance values:** speed_tol = 1 m/s, sin_tol = 1/2.\n- **holds:** the car goes clockwise; the cross product is −150 at every scene.\n- **fails:** the car goes counter-clockwise; the cross product is +150.\n- **blind:** the holds trace with the car's velocity and speed masked.\n\nThe contract spells out the formula exactly, so I declared no narrowings. The record had no errors. `task_result.md` is written in the working directory.",
